    32	## LB-004: Horizon-Tail Truncation
    33	
    34	Let
    35	\[
    36	\Delta_T(H)=\sup_a\sum_{t\le T}\mathbb E[a\,1\{H<\tau_t(a)\le T-t\}].
    37	\]
    38	For every fixed comparator \(a\), truncation loses exactly the summand above, while the learner's true reward pathwise dominates its truncated reward. Hence
    39	\[
    40	R_T\le R_T^H+\Delta_T(H).
    41	\]
    42	Combining with LB-001 and LB-002 gives the \(\Delta_T\)-sufficiency bound. Status: accepted.
