   168	## LB-013: Concatenated Same-Path Horizon-Oblivious Lower Bound
   169	
   170	Let
   171	\[
   172	M_i=\sum_{j<i}(N_j+2)=o(N_i),
   173	\]
   174	and define one deterministic path by blocks
   175	\[
   176	P_{M_i+1},\ldots,P_{M_i+N_i}=0,\quad
   177	P_{M_i+N_i+1}=1/2,\quad
   178	P_{M_i+N_i+2}=1.
   179	\]
   180	For a process-aware but horizon-oblivious policy, the zero-block actions are the same random variables when regret is evaluated at
   181	\[
   182	T_i^0=M_i+N_i+1,\qquad T_i^1=M_i+N_i+2.
   183	\]
   184	With
   185	\[
   186	X_i=\mathbb E\sum_{t=M_i+1}^{M_i+N_i}A_t1\{A_t<1/2\},\qquad
   187	Y_i=\mathbb E\sum_{t=M_i+1}^{M_i+N_i}A_t1\{A_t<1\},
