    54	## CE-007: Horizon/Process-Aware Oracle Collapse
    55	
    56	Status: accepted obstruction to any instance-wise necessity theorem under oracle quantifiers.
    57	
    58	For any exogenous law \(P\) and horizon \(T\), define
    59	\[
    60	V_T^P(a)=\mathbb E_P\sum_{t\le T}r_t(a).
    61	\]
    62	Choose an \(\varepsilon_T\)-optimizer of \(\sup_a V_T^P(a)\) and post it in every round. The learner's expected reward equals \(V_T^P(a_T)\), so its pseudo-regret is at most \(\varepsilon_T=o(T)\), regardless of \(\beta,\gamma,\Delta_T,\Gamma_T\), or any other tail statistic. This is not an algorithmic result unless the process law and horizon are known and approximate optimization is allowed.
