   254	# Iteration 5 Consolidation
   255	
   256	## Accepted Progress
   257	
   258	- Accepted the general two-threshold block lemma. For \(0<c_0<c_1\le1\), if the first \(N\) actions have the same law under continuations \(0^N,c_0\) and \(0^N,c_1\), then
   259	\[
   260	\max\{R_{c_0},R_{c_1}\}\ge N\frac{c_0(c_1-c_0)}{c_1}
   261	\]
   262	against comparator suprema. The coefficient is maximized at \(c_0=1/2,c_1=1\), giving the existing \(1/4\) constant.
   263	- This lemma cleanly unifies the finite two-continuation gadget, the universal/process-unaware concatenation, and the same-path horizon-oblivious prefix conflict, without changing their quantifier restrictions.
   264	
   265	## Candidate Routes
   266	
   267	- Develop the prefix-compatibility modulus \(\kappa_I(\mathcal U)\) as a local simultaneous-payoff feasibility gap. For zero-block thresholds \(\{c_0,c_1\}\), the finite-grid/limit calculation recovers \(c_0(c_1-c_0)/c_1\).
   268	- Prove finite-grid duality first, then add strict-threshold \(\eta\)-comparator limits.
   269	- State any regret-transfer theorem with same-prefix-law assumptions, an outside-surplus cap \(B_u\), and probability weighting for rare prefix events.
