   324	# Iteration 6 Consolidation
   325	
   326	## Accepted Progress
   327	
   328	- Promoted a conditional \(\kappa\)-transfer lemma as a reusable lower-bound bookkeeping tool. It requires same conditional prefix action laws, payoff factorization, comparator prefix lower bounds, outside-surplus caps, and probability weighting for rare prefix events.
   329	- Promoted the multi-threshold zero-block LP dual:
   330	\[
   331	\kappa(C)=\max_{\lambda\in\Delta(C)}
   332	\left(\mathbb E_\lambda C-\sup_a a\Pr_\lambda(C>a)\right).
   333	\]
   334	For arbitrary threshold laws on \([0,1]\), the local welfare-minus-posted-revenue gap is at most \(1/e\), approached by equal-revenue tails.
   335	- Recorded finite-grid strict-crossing caveats: grid \(\kappa\) lower-bounds only grid-restricted learners unless a dense-grid or \(\eta\)-comparator limit is taken.
   336	
   337	## Candidate Routes
   338	
   339	- Prove the sharp finite-support constant \(((m-1)/m)^m\) for the best \(m\)-threshold local gap, or demote it if the missing upper bound fails.
   340	- Lift multi-threshold \(\kappa(C)\) to universal block lower bounds and same-path horizon-oblivious lower bounds, with explicit old-reward and intermediate-round caps such as \(M_i+m_i=o(N_i)\).
   341	- Study known deterministic paths as simultaneous-prefix design problems to understand the process-aware horizon-oblivious regime.
   342	
   343	## Refuted Or Weakened Claims
   344	
   345	- A positive local \(\kappa\) remains insufficient by itself; suffix compensation and rare-prefix dilution must be controlled.
   346	- The dual distribution over thresholds is not a hard stochastic process under the current pseudo-regret. It is a minimax certificate over deterministic continuations.
   347	- The finite-\(m\) constant is not the value for every fixed \(m\)-threshold set; e.g. two thresholds \(\{0.9,1\}\) have gap \(0.09\), not \(1/4\).
