   644	# Iteration 10 Consolidation
   645	
   646	## Accepted Progress
   647	
   648	- Promoted a nonconstructive deterministic derandomization of the known-path \(1/e\) upper bound. There exists one fixed deterministic horizon-oblivious quote sequence \(a_t\in(e^{-1},1)\) such that, uniformly over every nonincreasing threshold sequence \(c_1\ge\cdots\ge c_n\),
   649	\[
   650	\sum_{t\le n}a_t1\{a_t<c_t\}
   651	\ge
   652	\sum_{t\le n}(c_t-e^{-1})_+
   653	-O(n^{2/3}\sqrt{\log n}).
   654	\]
   655	- Applying this to suffix maxima \(M_{t,T}=\max_{t<s\le T}P_s\) gives, for every deterministic exogenous path,
   656	\[
   657	R_T\le (T-1)/e+O(T^{2/3}\sqrt{\log T}).
   658	\]
   659	Together with the accepted same-path lower bound, the sharp worst-case limsup constant \(1/e\) now holds for deterministic horizon-oblivious policies as well as randomized ones, in the nonconstructive existence sense.
   660	
